The current array index validation in `deepCopy` only checks if the property keys match `/^\d+$/`. This allows non-standard numeric keys (such as `'01'` or out-of-bounds indices like `'2'` on an array of length 2) to bypass validation and be silently dropped during the copy phase. To prevent silent data loss and ensure strict array integrity, validate that all own keys (except `'length'`) are valid, dense indices within the range `0` to `input.length - 1`.

```suggestion
      const ownKeys = Object.getOwnPropertyNames(input);
      const indexSet = new Set<string>();
      for (const key of ownKeys) {
        if (key === 'length') continue;
        const num = Number(key);
        if (!/^\d+$/.test(key) || String(num) !== key || num >= input.length) {
          return rejectUnsupported('Array must not have non-index own property: ' + key);
        }
        indexSet.add(key);
      }
```
