The `deepFreeze` utility currently uses `Object.keys` to recursively freeze properties. However, `Object.keys` only returns enumerable string-keyed properties. If the object contains symbol-keyed or non-enumerable properties, they will not be recursively frozen. Since `deepFreeze` is a publicly exported utility, it should be robust and freeze all own keys using `Reflect.ownKeys`.

```suggestion
      for (const key of Reflect.ownKeys(val)) {
        freeze((val as Record<string | symbol, unknown>)[key]);
      }
```

