Also remove the redundant prototype check in validateObject (since isPlainObject already checked). But validateObject is now removed (canonical delegates to validateJsonValue). So canonical.ts no longer has validate/validateArray/validateObject/hasLoneSurrogate/isPlainObject. Good — removes duplication. canonical.ts becomes thin.

But canonical.ts still needs serialize(). Keep that. And canonicalize validates via validateJsonValue + surrogate walk. Actually if validateJsonValue rejects surrogates, no separate walk needed. But to be safe (in case validateJsonValue is called without surrogate check in some path), I'll add surrogate check to validateJsonValue. Let me do that.

Let me also handle the redundant prototype check: in validateJsonValue's validateJsonObject, remove the isPlainObject guard? No, validateJsonValue already checks isPlainObject before calling. Inside, the prototype check is redundant but harmless. I'll leave it (or remove). The reviewer's note about canonical's validateObject prototype check is moot after refactor.

