Actually, to demonstrate "second read" issue: create a Proxy where reading a property returns value X first time and value Y second time. validateJsonValue reads it once (during validation) → X. serialize reads it again → Y (if it re-reads original). But after fix, serialize reads from validated copy (which stored X). So if X != Y, the bug version would output Y, fixed version outputs X.

